# CDP Operator Proxy

**Invariant:** `operator-proxy episode ∧ agent_bus.request from Cowork ⇒ follow this rule before authoring DIRECTIVE bodies or dispositing CLOSEOUTs.`

**Skill homes (BINDING — do not mix planes):**

| Concern | Skill home | Who |
|---|---|---|
| Operator contract (DIRECTIVE/DISPOSITION, inv 30 streaming-stop auth, mission debrief) | `cdp-operator-proxy` (`shared_sync`) | Operator seat + IDE reviewing operator behavior |
| Cursor mechanism (admit gates, nest/lease, chip delivery) | `operator-proxy-substrate` (`cursor_only`) | Cursor seats only |
| CDP/Jupiter transport (poll ladder, CSE retain against **poller** kill, warm follow-up) | `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` (`cursor_only`) | Cursor seats — **poller plane**, not Opus self-stop |

`CSE retain` (navigation) ≠ `streaming-stop authorization` (operator-proxy inv 30). Diagnosing "stream stopped mid-mission" ⇒ load **both**: navigation for harness/poller, operator-proxy for leg-vs-mission and exception notify.

**Operator identity (BINDING):** `default(operator) = model_seat` — assume **non-human** unless operator **explicitly declares** human operator (skill invariant 0). Cowork CSE presence alone ≠ human operator.

**Streaming stop (BINDING — inv 30):** `end(CSE identity) ⇔ continuity_handoff ∨ TYPE:MISSION_CLOSEOUT`. **Tab ⟂ stream ⟂ lane** (`decision:cse-tab-decoupled-from-session`) — PARK / WAITING / stand-down may end the **stream** without ending CSE or bus lane; ¬ hop or re-stream to keep a tab warm. A leg DISPOSITION does **not** authorize `MISSION_CLOSEOUT`. **Persistent-lane carve-out:** on `bus_lifecycle:persistent` + long-lived operator, `MISSION_CLOSEOUT` only for true mission/arc end or forced CSE refresh — a landed roadmap row / work-unit complete is a Leg (do **not** emit MISSION_CLOSEOUT; stream MAY park). **Going-quiet ≡ stream-stop** on that lane (report WAITING / PARK; continue the **lane**, not the generate). **Self-scheduled wake:** arm **both** Monitor + `send_later` at **first dispatch** with work in flight; re-arm `send_later` every turn; tear down at true close. Wake bounds silence — does **not** prevent stopping. Wake notification is **not** the user (gates stay open). Monitor timeout ambiguity UNRESOLVED (armed 3600000 / reported 1800000 / docs say ignored when persistent). Reliability unprobed-from-cursor-sdk — not a hard SLA. Guide: `cortex://notes/system/specs/cdp-seat-wake-heartbeat.md`. First-dispatch inject: mission briefing (`operator_proxy_wake_brief`). Skill § Self-scheduled wake. Episodic exit-as-default is **not** retired. Unexpected stop ⇒ awareness `notify` tag `cse-stream-stop` (cursor fires if operator seat already quiet).

**Mission default (BINDING):** CDP Opus mission launch (`purpose=operator-proxy|mission` via `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…, purpose=…)` primary; IF6 = CLI `scripts/cortex/claude-ai-sync-jupiter project-ask`) ⇒ **Opus = operator · Fable = advisor · cursor/grok-4.6 = reasoner · cursor-auto = executor · tick = admitter**. Auto-inject on mission submit. Substrate hypotheses → reasoner (`contract: investigate`, inv 28). Fable escalate: prefer `team_dispatch(model=cdp/fable)`. Tick posting + B1/B2 nest stall: `cortex://notes/system/specs/cursor-auto-tick-work-posting.md`.

**Thread privacy:** operator-proxy DIRECTIVE/CLOSEOUT/DISPOSITION live on a **private `request` thread** — ¬ the IDE orchestrator’s endeavor root (cite root in `arc:` only).

**Two slugs (BINDING — `decision:operator-proxy-skill-surface-split`):** `cdp-operator-proxy` (`shared_sync`) = **operator contract** — what the operator seat executes. **Cursor seats** additionally bind `operator-proxy-substrate` (`cursor_only`) for admit gates, `nest_under` + lease, chip delivery, and CDP packet mechanics. Carve rule: `shared_body ⇒ observable behavior` · `code_body ⇒ mechanism`.

**Protocol SOT:** `cortex://notes/system/specs/cdp-operator-proxy-v0.md` (field tables, transport).  
**Doctrine:** `decision:operator-proxy-seat-posture`.  
**Transport sibling:** `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` for CDP/Jupiter mechanics (incl. warm same-CSE follow-up).

**Session abort (BINDING):** IDE/cursor lead **¬** cancel cursor-sdk dispatches or kill in-flight executions without **explicit operator authorization** for that session — poll, read closeout, paste status into live CDP converse; operator supersedes on private lane. MCP `project_ask` abort is gone. Rule: `in-flight-work-guard_ulg.mdc`.

**Operator restart (BINDING):** while Auto can claim, `agent_bus.request` with `contract: propagate` — cursor-auto mints propagation rows and coordinates drain-gated `sync_restart` (not tier-M `execute` + `manage.*`). **Auto wedged ⇒ `send(to=cursor)`** attended IDE (inv 40) — `propagate` enqueues on the broken slot. Skill § Blocked → ask ladder.

**Autonomy default (BINDING — inv 39):** `recovery_path=human` / manage outside `VALID_SERVICES` / no supervisor ⇒ implement autonomous recovery. ¬ operator-only gate · ¬ `TYPE: OPERATOR_GATE` · ¬ wake. tmux `0:0` is a seat recipe, not a human terminal.

**claude.ai and Cursor IDE are resilient to all service restarts (BINDING — 2026-08-13 / 2026-08-25):** includes `mcp` **and** `cdp_ask`. `drop(attach) ∧ ¬end(CSE ∨ IDE chat)`. Recover after `wait_healthy` (IDE: retry tools; CSE: followup/reattach by `chat_url`, or continuity hop for tooling chips). IDE/lead ¬ skip `mcp` or `cdp_ask` `sync_restart` citing “would drop Cowork attach” **or** “this session is in-flight” (`mcp_session_hot`). **Tab ⟂ session:** `open(tab) ⇏ alive(session ∨ stream)` — hop ≠ tab-keepalive (`decision:cse-tab-decoupled-from-session`). Rule: `restart-drain-discipline` § CSE vs service.

**Transport vs bus (BINDING):** `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` / `cse_session(followup)` = IDE↔Cowork converse transport; operator commission = **`agent_bus.request` on private request thread**. Killing a transport handle does **not** cancel bus work — poll the request lane, not `active_work` alone. Reconnect: `cse_session(op=followup)` same `holder` (Cowork CSE) **or** continue on bus thread (`mark_read` → next `request`).

## When

- Cowork holds operator seat driving cursor via `agent_bus.request`
- Authoring or reviewing `TYPE: DIRECTIVE` / `TYPE: DISPOSITION` turns
- cursor-auto nested dispatch arcs (5867-class dogfood)
- Blocked on a human/cursor fact — skill § Blocked → ask ladder (observe → cursor → Cowork Ask/push); ¬ silent stop
- Life missing a code-seat tool (`manage`, reload, …) — commission **cursor** (`request` if Auto can claim; `send(to=cursor)` if Auto is wedged — inv 40); ¬ park on the human
- **CSE stream stopped / mid-mission idle** — this rule (inv 30) **and** `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` (poller retain)

¬ load for IDE cursor lead orchestration (`lean-context-dispatch-first` + `operator-posture` instead).
IDE warm follow-up into live CSE: `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` § Warm follow-up (CDP into chat; ¬ bus-only + push).
